{
  "profile": "skulk.calls/1",
  "protocol": 1,
  "canonicalization": "skulk.portable-json/1",
  "composition_profile": "skulk.composition/1",
  "protected_hello_profile": "skulk.handshake/1",
  "media_profile": "skulk.transport/1",
  "limits": {
    "metadata_bytes": 262144,
    "payload_bytes": 16777216,
    "unary_seconds": 30,
    "stream_seconds": 300
  },
  "framing": "u32 big-endian metadata length; canonical metadata UTF-8; exactly payload_size raw bytes. No trailing bytes. Both bounds apply before allocation.",
  "semantics": [
    "This explicit new control profile is selected only by an admitted signed runtime cohort; no automatic downgrade or profile guessing. Issued managed, handshake, media and control profiles are unchanged.",
    "Invoke and delegate raw payloads must be portable JSON objects. Preserve their exact bytes and bind SHA-256 to the independently admitted composition context or delegate request. Canonicalizing metadata never reserializes payload bytes.",
    "Context parsing grants no authority. Only the authenticated host active-scope registry may admit a root or delegation and must match original caller, live connection, local call, exact destination, policy, monotonic deadline and cancellation tree.",
    "Parent-scoped delegation request_id is an increasing unsigned 64-bit sequence starting at one, encoded as 64 lowercase hexadecimal digits. Host permits at most one pending delegation per parent. Rejected admitted sequence numbers remain consumed; structural/racing requests do not advance it. No completed-ID ledger or total request allowance.",
    "Result and delegate_result carry a portable JSON object payload on success, and zero payload bytes on a bounded non-null error. Error messages never carry raw provider detail.",
    "Health, shutdown and cancel have zero payload bytes. Health surface identities and readiness keep the existing transport/1 semantics.",
    "One pending root invocation per managed child remains the declared concurrency rule. Cancellation, invalid/partial I/O, unknown execution outcome or channel loss never authorize retry or effect replay.",
    "A stream invocation negotiates its separate startup/call-bound media channel using the unchanged transport/1 framing and lifecycle. This control codec alone does not qualify stream routing or remote Fabric admission.",
    "Destination io_mode is pinned by the exact signed descriptor revision. Unary delegation has one delegate_result. A streaming delegation either fails with delegate_result before starting or receives one delegate_started followed by one delegate_finished; the host enforces that state machine.",
    "Only the host assigns delegate_started.media_call_id and binds its one-use media hello to the actual parent connection, parent call, request ID and active child scope. It must differ from the parent call ID. Frame parsing or a claimed media ID never establishes that binding.",
    "A caller must not expose successful stream completion until the media terminal/end, delegate_finished and required handler cleanup agree. Native media alone does not establish completion of its delegated call. Parent completion/cancellation retires all active children; early stream abandonment cancels the parent in this profile. No uncertain execution is replayed.",
    "The host clamps delegate_started.remaining_seconds to the active child monotonic budget. Callers additionally clamp against their existing parent budget and the supplied absolute deadline; a delayed control message cannot mint a fresh deadline."
  ],
